# Trivy ignore file
# Findings suppressed here are false positives or intentional design decisions.

# DS026: Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK
# Health checks for this workload are enforced by Kubernetes liveness, readiness,
# and startup probes defined in deployment.yaml. The Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK
# instruction is not executed by Kubernetes and is therefore not applicable.
AVD-DS-0026

# KSV013: image tag not pinned in deployment.yaml
# The image name and tag are set at deploy time by Kustomize (kustomization.yaml).
# The bare image name in deployment.yaml is intentional — it is the Kustomize target.
AVD-KSV-0013

# GCP0072 / GCP0074: firewall allows all ports / large port range
# The allow_internal_pods firewall rule intentionally allows all TCP/UDP ports
# within the pod and service CIDRs. This is required for arbitrary inter-pod
# communication. The security boundary is the source_ranges restriction to
# pod/service CIDRs only — not the public internet.
AVD-GCP-0072
AVD-GCP-0074

# GCP0050: node pool does not override default service account
# A dedicated, minimally-privileged service account (google_service_account.node_sa)
# is explicitly set on the node pool. Trivy cannot resolve the cross-resource
# reference statically when scanning node_pool.tf in isolation.
AVD-GCP-0050
